  "worked_solution": "The vertex is the \"turning point\" of the parabola. In an upwards parabola, like the one here, the vertex is the minimum point. So, the vertex of this parabola is $(3,-2).$\n\nThe axis of symmetry is the vertical line that passes through the vertex. Therefore, the axis of symmetry of this parabola is $x=3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217628/assets/f139192260875d5e988f30a64a7024f50d68337dbd4969d938f18aa62b850dd0.png)",
